{"availability":"available","full":"kunobi-ninja/kache","name":"kache","description":"Zero-copy, content-addressed Rust build cache for Rust, C/C++ and more. No copies, no wasted disk","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":1024,"forks":54,"created":"2026-02-15T19:43:57Z","updated":"2026-10-03T09:09:14Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kunobi.ninja/kache","topics":["build-cache","caching","ci","developer-tools","hardlinks","rust","s3","zero-copy"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":1024,"forks":54}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kache is a compiler cache for Rust, C/C++, and CUDA. It keys every compiler invocation by the content of its inputs, so a crate built once is restored instead of rebuilt in your next worktree, branch, or CI run. Outputs live in a local content-addressed store and can be shared through S3-compatible or filesystem remotes. Linux, macOS, and Windows are supported and release-tested."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kunobi-ninja/kache/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4e8cb359f436015c2e74e544cf6bc50570a0fc79c2b043b76a1207dda1697a70","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Kache is a compiler cache for Rust, C/C++, and CUDA. It keys every compiler invocation by the content of its inputs, so a crate built once is restored instead of rebuilt in your next worktree, branch, or CI run. Outputs live in a local content-addressed store and can be shared through S3-compatible or filesystem remotes. Linux, macOS, and Windows are supported and release-tested.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kun